# Markdown is hand-formatted (docs, ADRs, READMEs); leave Prettier out of it.
*.md

# Vendored verbatim from claude-project-kit (docs/PIPELINE-CONTRACT.md is the
# contract they render). Kept byte-identical to upstream so /sync-kit can tell a
# real drift from a reformat; they are machine-consumed, never hand-edited here.
schemas/*.json
delivery.example.json
templates/workflows/

# ...and the same files once activated. Activation is a `git mv` across the
# boundary above, so without this line a workflow silently changes formatting
# owner the moment it turns on. Today every template happens to be
# Prettier-clean, so nothing was reformatted — that is luck, not a property: a
# future /sync-kit bringing across a workflow that is NOT clean would get it
# reformatted on the way in, and a reformatted file can no longer be compared
# byte-for-byte against upstream, which is exactly how /sync-kit tells a real
# drift from a cosmetic one. Deliberately scoped to the vendored `pipeline-*`
# files — the rest of `.github/workflows/` is todoclaw's own and stays under
# Prettier.
.github/workflows/pipeline-*.yml

# Sibling git worktrees checked out inside the main checkout (docs/COLLABORATION.md).
# Prettier already skips these via its default .gitignore honouring — this entry makes the
# exclusion explicit and independent of that default, so `format:check` can never start
# reformatting another branch's tree.
.claude/worktrees/
